/T (If a nonexistent path is passed, open\(\) raises FileNotFoundError. The except clause wraps it in RuntimeError using raise ... from exc, preserving the original exception as the cause. The with statement closes the file automatically. The finally block is included to demonstrate the complete try structure; it is safe for cleanup that is not already handled by with.)
