/Title (a function becomes harder as the file grows. A package loads imported modules once per process and caches them in sys.modules; subsequent imports normally reuse the cached module. Import work is generally a one-time startup cost. Package memory includes the loaded module objects and their globals, usually modest compared with the benefits of separation. Runtime algorithm complexity is unchanged by the organisation.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1253 0 R
/Prev 1279 0 R
/First 1307 0 R
/Last 1307 0 R
/Count -1
>>
