/Title (Manual management can use try/finally: open the file, perform writes in try, and close it in finally. This gives the same O\(n\) time and O\(1\) extra streaming space as with. With guarantees cleanup automatically. If a single file is open and an error occurs, a correctly written try/finally version closes it; without finally, one file may remain open. The original code can leave the log open when write fails and can also leave the input file open because it is not managed with a context manager.)
